{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you handle permits with the City of Upper Arlington?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Upper Arlington has its own permitting office and inspection process, separate from the City of Columbus. We're registered with the City of Upper Arlington and have completed multiple permitted projects there. We pull all required permits, schedule inspections, and track the city's review timeline so it doesn't delay your project."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of remodeling projects do you complete in Upper Arlington?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We specialize in kitchen remodeling, bathroom remodeling, basement finishing, and whole-home renovations throughout Upper Arlington and the Columbus area."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you help open up a closed floor plan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. This is one of the most common requests we get in Upper Arlington. Most older UA homes have separated kitchens that can be opened to the main living area. We assess the structural situation, including load-bearing walls, beam requirements, and HVAC routing, and design a solution that creates the open layout you want without compromising the house."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you help with design selections?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Our process includes design guidance, material selections, layout planning, and detailed project coordination to help homeowners make confident decisions throughout the remodeling process."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you work on older Upper Arlington homes with plaster walls or unusual layouts?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, this is most of what we do in Upper Arlington. Homes built between the 1920s and 1970s often have plaster walls, older wiring that needs to be addressed, and structural surprises inside the walls. We plan for this in our scoping process and build contingencies into our estimates so you don't get caught off guard."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you handle the whole project, or do I need to hire separate contractors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We handle everything. Design, permits, demolition, framing, plumbing, electrical, tile, cabinetry, countertops, and painting are all coordinated through one team. You don't need to manage separate subcontractors or chase anyone down. One point of contact from start to finish."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a remodel take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Kitchen remodels typically take six to ten weeks from demo to final walkthrough. Bathroom remodels run three to five weeks. Timelines vary based on material lead times (cabinets especially) and the scope of plumbing or structural work. We build out a project schedule before construction starts so you know exactly what to expect week by week."}}
]}

